WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.509
If you want to learn how you can win a free
CZsWorld hoodie to keep you warm this holiday

00:00:03.509 --> 00:00:05.980
season then stick around to the end of this
video.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.519
Welcome to a very Merry episode of Things
You Missed, cause today we’re coving the

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:16.840
2006 version of Black Christmas.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.590
So really it’s not too Merry at all.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.470
If you’re looking for a happier holiday
video, go watch my episode on the original

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.560
movie, but if you’re staying here then let’s
get into the Things You Missed.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.280
[THINGS YOU MISSED]

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:32.090
At the beginning we see Claire writing in
red ink, drinking red wine… wait -- don’t

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.230
go in the closet Claire.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:34.230
Red means dead!

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.590
Don’t go in the -- why does nobody EVER
LISTEN TO ME!

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:40.010
In this movie we are shown a bit more backstory
about the killer, Billy.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.870
We first meet him confined in a facility known
as the Clark Sanitarium.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.010
This is an homage to Bob Clark, the man who
directed the original 1974 version of Black

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.829
Christmas, but that’s not the only tribute
to him in the movie.

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:53.350
Black Christmas is not the most well known
Christmas movie that Clark has directed, because

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.630
he also directed the comedy, A Christmas Story
in 1983.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:00.329
The most iconic prop from that movie, really
one of the most iconic props from any movie,

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:04.790
is the Leg Lamp that Mr. Parker wins in a
contest, much to the dismay of his wife.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.000
“I know just the place for it.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.170
Right in the middle of our front room window!”

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.170
“Uh?”

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.140
In Black Christmas, the lamp can be seen in
the background in the girls’ living room.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.060
But that’s not the only A Christmas Story
reference seen in the movie.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.770
When Ralphie finally gets his BB gun for Christmas
and shoots his eye out, his glasses end up

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.580
saving him, so he makes up a story for his
Mom about how an icicle came down and broke

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:26.710
the spectacles.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:27.840
Roll it.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.110
“And I tried to get out of the way.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.320
But I..."

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.420
"There. See? It's just a little bump.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.060
You're OK.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.860
You're lucky it didn't cut your eye,

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.240
those icicles have been known to kill people.”

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:45.010
Well there just so happens to be one victim
in Black Christmas who isn’t murdered by

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:47.580
anyone, but rather falls prey to a deadly
icicle.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.210
That’s Mrs. Mac, the house mother.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:53.010
She’s played by Andrea Martin, who graduated
to that role after playing one of the sorority

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.119
girls, Phyl, back in the original Black Christmas.

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:58.810
This next one isn’t my own discovery, but
I saw something online about it so I thought

00:01:58.810 --> 00:01:59.810
I’d give it a mention.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.970
Each one of the girls is named after a singer
who made a well known Christmas song:

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.780
Kelli Presley for Elvis Presley

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.260
Melissa Kitt for Eartha Kitt

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.320
Dana Mathis for Johnny Mathis

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.080
Clair Crosby for Bing Crosby

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.340
Leigh Colvin for Shawn Colvin

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:32.420
Megan Helms for Bobby Helms

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:36.860
And finally….

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.200
Heather Fitzgerald for Ella Fitzgerald

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:46.080
I think that’s enough Christmas music for... for like ever.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.330
One thing that this remake does that I liked
was have elements of the original, but the

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.720
script is totally different.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.480
Some of those elements include Agnes and Billy,

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.260
using plastic wrap for a kill, having the

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:06.110
killer setup shop in the attic, using the
disturbing phone calls made from inside the

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:09.970
house to frighten the girls (this time using
each victim’s cell phone because those exist

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:10.460
now)

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.500
"Can you hear me now?"

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.200
*horror screams*

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.240
"Good."

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.099
...the weapon used in Billy’s most iconic
kill from the original movie is shown to be

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.410
a gift given in the girls’ secret Santa
exchange…

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:24.280
“Oh thanks Eve.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.500
That’s… that’s so sweet.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.160
On a side note, Eve is the name of the girl
who delivers the murder weapon on Christmas

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.170
Eve?

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.980
That sounds possibly intentional but not really that
interesting.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.830
And most notably, making the killers obsessed
with eyes and peepholes to give more meaning

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:40.060
to the most iconic shot from the original.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:43.550
Eyes continue to show up throughout the movie
for seemingly no reason though, like some

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.530
of the wall artwork and Megan’s screensaver.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:46.970
Speaking of Megan’s computer…

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:50.460
I don’t think it’s entirely clear what
is going on when Kyle shows up, so let me

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.770
run though that subplot really quick.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:53.420
Kyle is shown to be dating Kelly.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.450
When she gets out of the car, he gets on the
phone with Megan.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.989
We don’t hear the conversation, but we later
see Kyle in a video with Megan.

00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:02.050
Let’s just say it would end up in the adult
section of the video store had it been the

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.080
pre-internet days.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.300
Kyle probably doesn’t want his girlfriend
to find out, so we can assume that’s what

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.599
the earlier argument was about.

00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:11.560
He later climbs into Megan’s room, probably
to confront her about it, maybe to steal back

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.330
the video, but he gets caught, and tells his
girlfriend he was trying to climb into her

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:18.329
room, but the window was closed, so he went
into Megan’s instead.

00:04:18.329 --> 00:04:21.779
Then in the background, and this is only on
screen for a moment, it seems that Megan has

00:04:21.779 --> 00:04:25.979
posted the video on a message board called
C Pupils, which I guess specializes in home

00:04:25.979 --> 00:04:27.860
made videos from college students.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:31.780
The users of this site look like perfectly
normal, well-adjusted individuals.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.740
Also, one other note on Megan’s room, she
has this poster for a Raveonettes concert

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:43.849
with an insane looking depiction of the male
/ female rock duo, a clue that the antagonists

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:47.900
of this movie would also be a mentally depleted
guy / girl team: Billy and Agnes.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.380
When we see into Billy's childhood the first present he gets is a satellite.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:54.819
and the other one is a telescope,
both things that fit into the theme of surveillance

00:04:54.819 --> 00:04:55.819
and voyeurism.

00:04:55.819 --> 00:04:59.589
We see how Billy gets his peephole kink from
a very young age, he watches his parents fight

00:04:59.589 --> 00:05:01.930
through door cracks and holes in the architecture.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:05.150
When Heather find the collection of newspapers
hidden in the wall, there’s an article about

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.370
the night that Billy attacked his family on
Christmas, where we see the origin of the

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.370
movie’s title.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.430
The massacre was dubbed by the media as “Black
Christmas”.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.280
After Kelly and Leigh make it out of the house
to the hospital, is what I think is the most

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.050
horrifying part of the movie.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.979
I mean I guess they felt like they had to fit in
the Christmas carolers from the original film

00:05:19.979 --> 00:05:23.740
somehow, so they got a bunch of grown
adults dressed like some steampunk 1930s lookin

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.480
thing and THIS!?

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.020
I mean this should be the killer.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.020
This is terrifying!

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:32.129
I anyway, I don’t have anything else for
this one, if you haven’t seen it, it’s

00:05:32.129 --> 00:05:34.840
more gross than it is scary, so I’m not
really into that.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:38.330
But I do have something for you, it’s
a little holiday gift to keep you warm during

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.770
your Christmas-horror movie marathons this
December.

